  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xA9A9" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Hot-Intake Idle Threshold [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x13F88; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Threshold of the hot-intake idle latch in FUN_00059C2C, looked up by the coolant byte 0xFFFF1069 while the knock state 0xFFFF23C6.bit6 is clear. The interpolated value goes to 0xFFFF34FA, and 0xFFFF4569.bit5 sets when 0xFFFF268C, plus ROM8[0x85D6] = 3 while the bit is set, reaches it. 0xFFFF455B.bit7, the hot-intake idle request of the VVEL modes 12 and 13, requires this latch. Stock 255, 255, 255, 255, 255, 130, 110, 90. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x13f88 bound to accessor 0x59c2c through literal 0x59d90. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x counts of 0xFFFF268C; proposed editor-grid inverse x. Origin: the byte comparison in FUN_00059C2C. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
