  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x8B2" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Running [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16BB4; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 15 duration target of the VVEL selector: the normal running mode above idle without a hot-intake or throttled request. The resolver interpolates it by engine speed and scales the count by the float literal 0.005 before the selector publishes the command. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16bb4 bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x56680, accessor 0x56dca through literal 0x56f78. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.005 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.005. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505, vvel_duration_running_axis/axis. The encoded arithmetic factor is not the physical duration unit. The float literal is a binary value described by its nominal decimal factor, not a measurement of degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x5658C and by FUN_00056DCA at 0x56E1E, both through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x28320 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6 (3.125 RPM per count). The 0.005 factor is the float literal 0x3BA3D70A at 0x56690; the unit of the scaled duration is a vendor-catalog candidate. Mode assignment and selector logic are in JK78C.vvel.md. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
