  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5717" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Limit - Engine Speed [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x160BA; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Engine-speed curve of the shaft-angle bound applied in the task before the command conversion: the bound word is the curve value minus abs(0xFFFF5E8E). Values are in the shaft-angle domain of axis 0x000156DC. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x160ba bound to accessor 0x54fd0 through literal 0x552ac. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the task FUN_00054FD0 at callsite 0x550EC through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x282F4 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6 into 0xFFFF31BA. The 1/512 degree domain follows from the conversion pair; the bound composition is in JK78C.vvel.md. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
