  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7A97" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Throttled [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16D14; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 4 duration target of the VVEL selector: the throttled mode 0xFFFF4565.bit6 of FUN_0005A314, which, unless 0xFFFF4573.bit4 is set, is requested while booster vacuum is low or not yet sufficient, while the brake input is set without 0xFFFF23BD bit 5 or bit 4 or at a speed byte of 253 or more, or while bit 7 of 0xFFFF5FCA or 0xFFFF5FCD is set; and the cold path after 2000 passes with 0xFFFF23B8.bit6, the per-pass latch of the CLSD THL POS status 0xFFFF23B9.bit6 (DID 0x1302 bit 0). Interpolated by engine speed and scaled by 0.05. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16d14 bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x569cc, accessor 0x657e4 through literal 0x6645c, accessor 0x657e4 through literal 0x66698. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. The 0.05 multiplication, offset arithmetic and shared dispatcher word domain do not establish physical duration degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x566BA through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x28320 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6, and by FUN_000657E4 at three callsites with the same axis. The resolver loads the literal from the pool at 0x569CC that follows FUN_0005693A. The 0.05 factor is the float literal 0x3D4CCCCC; the duration unit is a vendor-catalog candidate. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
