  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4184" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Hot Intake Idle [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0xE1CE; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 12 duration surface of the VVEL selector: hot-intake idle (0xFFFF455B.bit7) with the high-detonation state 0xFFFF23C6.bit6 clear. The mode value is the maximum of this surface and the eight-point floor 0x0001600A, scaled by 0.05. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0xe1ce bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x566a0. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. Coordinate semantics and maximum composition do not establish degrees for the ordinate. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x565D8 through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28058 with r7 = 0xFFFF11A6 on the first axis and the stack coordinate max(0, torque word 0xFFFF2E26) on the second axis. Both axes are reached from the GBR base literal 0x00015FFA at 0x56678. Stock values are identical to the knock surface 0x0000E24E. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
