  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1FFA" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Limit - Intake CVTC Angle [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16A74; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Intake-cam-angle curve of the shaft-angle bound applied in the task before the command conversion: the bound falls from 31.0 degrees at zero advance to 12.8 degrees at 75 degrees of advance. Values are in the shaft-angle domain of axis 0x000156DC. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16a74 bound to accessor 0x54fd0 through literal 0x555b0. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the task FUN_00054FD0 at callsite 0x552EA through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x28320 indexed by min(0xFFFF23A0, 0xFFFF23A2), the lower of the two bank cam-angle words in the 0x8000-centered domain. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
