  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x344E" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Hot Intake Idle, Knock [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0xE24E; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 13 duration surface of the VVEL selector: hot-intake idle with the high-detonation state 0xFFFF23C6.bit6 set. The mode value is the maximum of this surface and the eight-point floor 0x0001601A, scaled by 0.05. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0xe24e bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x566ac. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. A knock-state selector and identical stock bytes do not establish physical duration degrees. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x5664A through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28058 with the same coordinates and axes as the mode 12 surface 0x0000E1CE. Stock values are identical to that surface; only the knock state selects between them. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
