  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xD388" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Monitor Floor - A [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1609A; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. First engine-speed floor of the expected control-shaft angle: FUN_000BF0C0 and FUN_000BF122 take the maximum of the four floor words 0xFFFF3276, 0xFFFF3278, 0xFFFF380A, and 0xFFFF380C, this curve, floor B, and their second copies, then subtract the measured angle 0xFFFF2670 and clamp at zero into 0xFFFF2B2E. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x1609a bound to accessor 0x54fd0 through literal 0x55294. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the task FUN_00054FD0 at callsite 0x550C0 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x282F4 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6 into 0xFFFF3276. The subtraction from the 1/512 degree angle word 0xFFFF2670 fixes the domain. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
