  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4D4" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Monitor Floor - B [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x160AA; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Second engine-speed floor of the expected control-shaft angle, combined with floor A by maximum in FUN_000BF0C0 and FUN_000BF122 before the deficit against the measured angle 0xFFFF2670 is formed. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x160aa bound to accessor 0x54fd0 through literal 0x552a4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the task FUN_00054FD0 at callsite 0x550D6 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x282F4 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6 into 0xFFFF3278. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
