  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xF034" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Command Word - Shaft Angle Conversion, Second Copy</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1B00A; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Second copy of the shaft-angle conversion, read only by FUN_0004FCB8: it converts the two measured control-shaft angle words 0xFFFF2670 and 0xFFFF2672 to the command-word domain and publishes the mean of the two results times 1/512 as the float 0xFFFF9E98 for FUN_0004F3FE. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x1b00a bound to accessor 0x4fcb8 through literal 0x4fd84 + 0x20. Read by FUN_0004FCB8 at callsites 0x4FCD0 and 0x4FCDE through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x28510 of the kernel 0x289AC as GBR + 0x20 from the literal 0x0001AFEA at 0x4FD84; the primary conversion 0x000156FC goes through the wrapper 0x28320. FUN_0004F3FE is the only caller and the only reader of the float. The two argument words are the measured angles that the deficit monitors FUN_000BF0C0 and FUN_000BF122 subtract from the floor maximum. Stock bytes are identical to the primary table 0x000156FC.</description>
