  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7D78" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Cold [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16A54; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 3 duration target of the VVEL selector: the cold branch taken while the coolant snapshot 0xFFFFA21A or the selected-temperature snapshot 0xFFFFA219 is below 70 degC. Interpolated by coolant temperature and scaled by 0.05. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16a54 bound to accessor 0x56a14 through literal 0x56c88. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. The coolant-coordinate proof does not prove the duration output unit. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by FUN_00056A14 at callsite 0x56A2A through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x282F4; the base literal 0x00016A54 at 0x56C88 also reaches the axis at + 0x70 and the cold CVTC curve at + 0x40. The coordinate is the coolant byte 0xFFFF1069 (degC + 50). Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
