  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x9F13" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Shaft Angle Monitor Floor - B, Second Copy [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1B29A; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Second copy of monitor floor B: FUN_00059B64 interpolates it by the word 0xFFFF11BC into 0xFFFF380C, one of the four floor words 0xFFFF3276, 0xFFFF3278, 0xFFFF380A, and 0xFFFF380C whose maximum the deficit monitors FUN_000BF0C0 and FUN_000BF122 compare with the measured control-shaft angle. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x1b29a bound to accessor 0x59b64 through literal 0x59ba8. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x/512 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x*512. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:491-499, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:525-530, vvel_shaft_angle_axis/axis, vvel_command_shaft_angle/tbl. A shared integer domain, maximum, subtraction, absolute-value correction or word bound preserves count arithmetic. None independently fixes 512 counts per physical degree. An RPM or CVTC input grid cannot establish the returned shaft-coordinate unit. The upstream coordinate scale itself has no physical grounding in the finite sources. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by FUN_00059B64 at callsite 0x59B72 through the 8-point uint16 wrapper 0x282F4. No direct call reaches the reader; its entry address is the word at 0x21BBC of a function-pointer list. The maximum with the primary floor words fixes the 1/512 degree domain. Stock bytes are identical to the primary table 0x000160AA. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
