  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x29FD" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration State Word - Hot Intake Idle [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x102CE; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Duration word surface of the state-code dispatcher FUN_000657E4 for state code 5; FUN_0004692A assigns code 5 to VVEL mode 12, code 6 to mode 13, and code 7 to mode 14 from the published mode byte 0xFFFF2808; mode 14 is unreachable on JK78C, so code 7 is never produced. The dispatcher evaluates the state bytes 0xFFFF43F2 and 0xFFFF4480 in turn and publishes the duration word 0xFFFF122C. Stock values span 900..1180 = 45.0..59.0. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x102ce bound to accessor 0x657e4 through literal 0x66670. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-441, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:478-505. The common word-domain channel supports a numeric relationship to the throttled curve, not a physical degree unit or execution of a float multiply at this lookup. The returned table quantity is distinct from its axis-coordinate quantity and from the paired command-word domain. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by FUN_000657E4 at callsites 0x664B8 and 0x66578, where r4 holds the surface selected before the call through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28058 with r7 = min(0xFFFF, 0xFFFF11AC &lt;&lt; 2), the latched 12.5 RPM per count engine-speed word in the 3.125 RPM domain on the first axis and the stack coordinate the load byte 0xFFFF1032 &lt;&lt; 8, the byte that indexes the ignition mode surfaces in FUN_00069AB8 on the second axis. The same dispatcher takes the throttled curve 0x00016D14 for state codes 1 and 3, so the word shares the 0.05 domain of that curve. The resolver pair of modes 12 and 13 is a separate pair of surfaces with its own axes. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
