    <title>VVEL Duration State Word - Idle Model and Running [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x100CE; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Duration state word of the state codes 2 and 8 (VVEL modes 5 and 15) in the state-code dispatcher FUN_000657E4, looked up by min(0xFFFF, 0xFFFF11AC &lt;&lt; 2) over the axis 0x00016C84 and by the load byte 0xFFFF1032 &lt;&lt; 8 over the axis 0x00016C24. On the stock path, ROM8[0x8966].bit4 set (0x50), the dispatcher reads it for the current code 0xFFFF43F2 and for the previous code 0xFFFF4480 and publishes the duration word 0xFFFF122C; the codes 1 and 3 read 0x00016D14 instead. The path for the bit clear also reads it. Stock 660..1440 = 33.0..72.0. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x100ce bound to accessor 0x657e4 through literal 0x66684. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*0.05 deg; proposed editor-grid inverse x/0.05. Origin: the 0.05 duration scale of the state words in defs/JK78C.vvel.md. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
