  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xF7E1" flags="0x0">
    <title>End of Injection Angle - Base</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x15F22; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Base end-of-injection angle over an explicit eight-point engine-speed axis. The injection writer interpolates the eight uint16 cells, adds one or two correction bytes, and stores 2*min(sum, 209) to the end-of-injection word, the delay in 2 crank degrees per count from the reference tooth of the scheduled channel to the end of the pulse. A cell of x counts ends the pulse 4*x - 590 degrees after the following intake TDC, as a cell of JK08A 00012302 does. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x15f22 bound to accessor 0x730cc through literal 0x73518. Writer 000730cc loads the curve from literal 00073518 for the calls at 0007335e and 000733a2 to wrapper 000282f4 on axis 00015f32 and engine-speed word ffff11ac. It adds byte ffff35d3, and on the second call also byte ffff310f, before the clamp, and stores the result to ffff192a.</description>
