  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEFF3" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Characteristic [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x15AA2; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Monotonic duration characteristic of the VVEL duration ratio correction. FUN_00055E78 looks up this curve with its lookup duration x512, clamped below 128.0, over the axis 0x00017004 and stores the value at 2^-18 per count in 0xFFFFA0D8. FUN_00055F2C and FUN_00055FF2 each clamp the ratio 0xFFFF365A / max(0xFFFF3332, 1) to their own bounds, scale the curve value by it, and look up the axis 0x00017004 over this curve to obtain a corrected duration. FUN_00055F2C clamps to ROM16[0x921E] .. ROM16[0x9220] * 2^-13 = 0 .. 0, so its corrected duration is the first axis point 25.0; FUN_00055FF2 clamps to ROM16[0x9222] .. ROM16[0x9224] * 2^-13 = 65535 / 8192 for both bounds, so its corrected duration has 7.9999 times the characteristic of the lookup duration, capped at the last axis point 95.0. The stock cells rise from 1016 to 38435 and hold 38435 from the eleventh point (73.0). Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x15aa2 bound to accessor 0x55e78 through literal 0x56084, accessor 0x55ff2 through literal 0x562ec. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x*2^-18; proposed editor-grid inverse x*2^18. Origin: the float literal 2^-18 at 0x56090. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
