  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5067" flags="0x0">
    <title>End of Injection Angle - Conditional</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x15F42; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Conditionally selected end-of-injection angle over the engine-speed axis of the base curve. The injection writer interpolates the eight uint16 cells and stores 2*min(y, 209) of the interpolated value y, without correction bytes, to the end-of-injection word, the delay in 2 crank degrees per count from the reference tooth of the scheduled channel to the end of the pulse. A cell of x counts ends the pulse 4*x - 590 degrees after the following intake TDC, as a cell of JK08A 0001230a does. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x15f42 bound to accessor 0x730cc through literal 0x732f4. Writer 000730cc loads the curve from literal 000732f4 for the call at 000731c0 to wrapper 000282f4 on axis 00015f32 and engine-speed word ffff11ac while ffff4531.bit6 and ffff23e3 bits 2 and 3 are set, and stores twice the clamped value to ffff192a.</description>
