  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xC6A4" flags="0x0">
    <title>Target Mixture - Main</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0xA3CA; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Target mixture map: Q7 fuel-multiplier command against the stoichiometric base schedule (commanded equivalence ratio x/128), 128 = closed-loop stoichiometric target, 149 = 1.16. Stage 0005594a looks it up on engine speed (axis 00011cc0, rpm/50 against word ffff11bc) and load (axis 00011ac7, normalized BFS Q7 from ffff102c, or 0xff while wide-open latch ffff2468 bit 3 holds), scales the deviation from 128 by 00012552 when ffff2466 bit 6 selects the high-detonation surface, and publishes the byte as ffff15eb and, through enrichment latch ffff24a2 bit 7 and the ramp of ffff123a, as commanded mixture ffff22e8 = byte &lt;&lt; 7. Public HR A2L name Target AFR Map (8x8) with gasoline scale 1881.6/x on axes Cylinder Filling Up Efficiency (x*0.78125 percent) and Engine Speed (x*50); the AFR scale is a candidate, the Q7 ratio and the stoichiometric neutral are code. Three 2026-08-26 vehicle recordings match the lookup in 98.3..100 percent of settled records. Result disposition: consumer. Definition address projected from JK08A 0000a9aa through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: target mixture stage 00071dfa repeats source stage 0005594a instruction for instruction and passes this literal with RPM word ffff11ac and normalized-load snapshot ffff1032 to the homologous explicit-axis wrapper 00027f58.</description>
