  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4541" flags="0x0">
    <title>Intake CVTC Target - Running [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16DC4; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 15 intake-cam target of the VVEL selector: the VTC half of the normal running pair, interpolated by engine speed. Zero at raw 0x8000, 0.5 per count. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16dc4 bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x5668c. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: (x-32768)*0.5 degCA; proposed editor-grid inverse x*2+32768. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-428, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:495-505, intake_cvtc_target_running_axis/axis. The resolver arithmetic establishes a centered numeric output only where the recorded conversion path is given. It does not establish physical camshaft/crankshaft degrees. Uniform zero counts cannot prove a slope. A proved RPM or temperature coordinate does not prove the table output unit. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x565A6 through the 16-point uint16 wrapper 0x28320 indexed by 0xFFFF11A6 and converted with the float literals 0xC6800000 (-16384) and 0x3F000000 (0.5). Degrees of cam advance are a vendor-catalog candidate for the scaled value. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
