    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x108CE; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 4 intake-cam target of the VVEL selector: the VTC half of the throttled pair, interpolated by engine speed and load. Zero at raw 0x8000, 0.5 per count. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x108ce bound to accessor 0x564a4 through literal 0x569d4. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: (x-32768)*0.5 degCA; proposed editor-grid inverse x*2+32768. Origin: the retained layout interpretation and defs/JK78C.vvel.md:409-428, defs/JK78C.vvel.md:495-505. The resolver arithmetic establishes a centered numeric output only where the recorded conversion path is given. It does not establish physical camshaft/crankshaft degrees. Uniform zero counts cannot prove a slope. A proved RPM or temperature coordinate does not prove the table output unit. Recorded code and catalog interpretation: Read by the resolver FUN_000564A4 at callsite 0x566DE through the 16x16 uint16 wrapper 0x28090 with r7 = 0xFFFF11A6 on the first axis and the load fraction 0xFFFF238A on the second axis; the literals are in the pool at 0x569D4 that follows FUN_0005693A. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
