  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4685" flags="0x0">
    <title>Intake CVTC - Settle Countdown Reload [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x14230; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Load value of the countdown byte 0xFFFF24BF of the intake CVTC stage FUN_000E7FB4, selected while ROM8[0x852A] bit 0 is set and looked up over the axis 0x00013392 by byte 0xFFFF10F1. The stage loads the countdown and sets 0xFFFF23EC bit 3 when 0xFFFF23CB bit 7 and 0xFFFF2403 bit 2 are set, the target word 0xFFFF227C is at least ROM8[0x8B44] - 128 = 6 counts above 0x8000, the countdown 0xFFFF24C0 is zero, and the bit is clear. A lower target, either bit clear, or both word pairs 0xFFFF1AA6/0xFFFF1C1A and 0xFFFF1AA8/0xFFFF1C1C apart by more than ROM8[0x8B6C] = 14 reloads 0xFFFF24C0 from ROM8[0x8A5D] = 70 instead. The stage clears the bit once 0xFFFF24BF is zero while 0xFFFF23B8 bit 6 is set. The initializer FUN_000E56D4 loads 0xFFFF24BF from this curve by the live byte 0xFFFF1171 and 0xFFFF24C0 from ROM8[0x8A5D]. The routine that counts the two bytes down is not identified. Every stock cell holds 5; stock ROM8[0x852A] = 0x05 selects this curve. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x14230 bound to accessor 0xe56d4 through literal 0xe5900, accessor 0xe7fb4 through literal 0xe81c0. Engineering conversion is unestablished. Retained hypothesis: x counts of the countdown 0xFFFF24BF; proposed editor-grid inverse x. Origin: the byte store of FUN_000E7FB4 at 0x000E815E. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
