  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x367" flags="0x0">
    <title>Knock Threshold by Evaluator Channel</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x11F4E; 6 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence candidate. Knock Slice Map: per-evaluator-channel knock threshold by engine speed. A calculated metric exceeding the interpolated threshold contributes to increasing the knock count. On 7mfk, 00049ffc selects one of six one-based evaluator rows, interpolates 16 uint16 cells along axis 00015340, and writes the selected word at ffff2144 + 2*(c-1). Its bounded domain is 1 &lt;= c &lt;= 6; the accessor has no channel guard. JK08A stock rows 3 and 5 contain raw threshold 65535 at every cell. The selected raw word enters comparison in 0004a238; metric production, comparison outcome and count publication are outside the bounded lookup proof. Both neighboring cells are loaded, including 0001114e on the last row endpoint. The catalog identifies rows as cylinders, but exact lookup code does not establish physical cylinder or sensor order. The engineering threshold scale remains candidate. Definition address projected from JK08A 0001108e through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: exact normalized accessor shape preserves the direct-row-major table operand.</description>
