    <title>Gear Transition Request - Reference Multiplier [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16464; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-word reference multiplier indexed by min(current-gear index uint8[ffff1076],7) while ffff4563.bit3 is set, otherwise by min(target-gear index uint8[ffff1077],7). The latched gear indices follow defs/JK78C.vvel.md, section "Data flow". The low 32-bit product with uint16[ffff10d2] is arithmetically shifted right five and divided by 25; the result is capped by ROM16[0000911e], floored by ROM16[0000918c] and stored at ffff3492. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16464 bound to accessor 0x96ce0 through literal 0x97168. Stock JK78C leaves the conditioner unexecuted: dispatcher 0009679a calls it only while bit 0 of ROM8[00008383] and bit 7 of the mode flags ROM8[00008968] are clear, and the flags hold 0x80. The receive table carries no frame 0x174 record, so the latched gear indices do not diverge. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
