    <title>Gear Transition Request - Rate - Current below Target + 2 [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0xB3AA; 4 rows x 4 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Selected rate surface when the special branch is inactive and the latched current-gear index uint8[ffff1076] &lt; min(target-gear index uint8[ffff1077]+2,255). Coordinates are min(uint16[ffff10be]&gt;&gt;3,255) and the target-gear index uint8[ffff1077] of defs/JK78C.vvel.md, section "Data flow". The byte result is multiplied by ten before the signed request-update calculation. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0xb3aa bound to accessor 0x96ce0 through literal 0x97194. Stock JK78C leaves the conditioner unexecuted: dispatcher 0009679a calls it only while bit 0 of ROM8[00008383] and bit 7 of the mode flags ROM8[00008968] are clear, and the flags hold 0x80. The receive table carries no frame 0x174 record, so the latched gear indices do not diverge. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
