    <title>Gear Transition Request - Recovery Decrement [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x158D2; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-word recovery array indexed by min(latched target-gear index uint8[ffff1077],7), as described in defs/JK78C.vvel.md, section "Data flow". When the selected recovery byte is zero, subtract the unsigned entry from signed state ffff36b0 with a -32768 floor, then publish the maximum of that state and the independently bounded current candidate at ffff36ae. The inactive-transition path forces the recovery byte to zero; the active path uses the target-gear index ffff1077, which can also be zero. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x158d2 bound to accessor 0x96ce0 through literal 0x97418. Stock JK78C leaves the conditioner unexecuted: dispatcher 0009679a calls it only while bit 0 of ROM8[00008383] and bit 7 of the mode flags ROM8[00008968] are clear, and the flags hold 0x80. The receive table carries no frame 0x174 record, so the latched gear indices do not diverge. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
