  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6C12" flags="0x0">
    <title>Engine Speed Limit - Throttle Request - Oil Temperature</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x16C14; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Eight-word oil-temperature threshold of the rotational-speed request limiter, read through 000282f4 on the explicit word axis 00016a64, which it shares with rev_limit_fuel_cut_curves/tbl. Its coordinate is rev_fuel_cut_selector/ram at ffff10e5, the filtered raw oil-thermistor code. While ffff4573.bit4 is set, the word published at ffff1a3c can lower the calibrated threshold, and it also bounds the downward threshold ramp. Producer 000bdf90 sets that bit by a hysteretic comparison of the code with ROM8[00008aef] and ROM8[00008af0] and leaves it clear while the oil-sensor fault records are set. This curve has no scalar-to-curve binding to the canonical alternate threshold. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x16c14 bound to accessor 0x94d6c through literal 0x95054. Stock JK78C applies the curve: bit 0 of ROM8[0000852a] enables the oil sensor, producer 000bdf90 compares the code with ROM8[00008aef] = 20 and hysteresis ROM8[00008af0] = 1, and the reader tests ffff4573.bit4. On the stock oil-thermistor curve 000140c4, codes 15, 16, 17, 18, 19 and 20 read about 151, 147, 144, 141, 138 and 136 C [cand]; the stock curve lowers the threshold to 5632 at code 17 and below and to 7552 at codes 18 and 19, and holds 9600 at code 20.</description>
