    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x135F0; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Stock-inert offset of the upper limit of the warm DFCO-transition timing-state addend 0x000137E8. When ROM8[0x8966].bit0 is set, FUN_000644D0 stores the centered addend, lookup minus 0x80, in 0xFFFF14E6, looks up this eight-point curve by the engine-speed byte 0xFFFF11A3 over the axis 0x00013C6A and stores the centered value in 0xFFFF1318, forms the limit signed8(0xFFFF1980) + (curve - 0x80) + high8(0xFFFF233E), saturates it to -128..127 in 0xFFFF14F0, and writes the smaller of the centered addend and the limit to 0xFFFF14E5. With bit 0 clear, it writes the centered addend unchanged. Stock ROM8[0x8966] = 0x50 keeps bit 0 clear, and every stock cell holds 0x80. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x135f0 bound to accessor 0x644d0 through literal 0x6483c, accessor 0x67122 through literal 0x673ac. Stock lookup status: unqualified. The periodic timing-state compositor reads this offset only on its RAM-selected branch, whose stock state producer remains unqualified. On JK78C the separate DFCO-transition reader has ROM8[00008966].bit0 clear in stock; that disabled caller does not establish inactivity of the shared calibration. Stock activation remains unqualified under issue #129. Stored counts are retained. Physical quantities and engineering conversions are unresolved. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
