    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x137F0; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Alternate warm DFCO-transition eight-point timing-state addend. It shares the index byte and the interpolator of the projected default table and is selected when the transition-completion latch is set. Common-definition Map 1 uses the canonical stock storage. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x137f0 bound to accessor 0x644d0 through literal 0x6484c. Both eight-point branches read the same index byte, so neither carries an engine-bank identity. The selector is the transition-completion latch: it sets when the normalized transition progress reaches 1.0 (0x8000) and releases below 0.898 (0x7300), and the default arm is the branch taken while the latch is clear.</description>
