  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xF505" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 4 - Fuel Compensation - Main - Alternate [stored count]</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1D900; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Alternate fuel-compensation surface selected by state code 2, derived from VVEL input mode 5. The selected channel replaces the default surface at full current-state weight. The physical unit, engineering conversion and neutral value are unestablished. Common-definition Map 4 storage is projected from 0x9FBA. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. Exact JK78C target-native table at 0x9fba bound to accessor 0x2f596 through literal 0x2febc, accessor 0x40958 through literal 0x40f70. Coordinator 0x00040958 selects this surface instead of the default fuel-compensation surface for state code 2 (VVEL input mode 5). At full current-state weight, changes to the default surface are replaced by this channel. During a transition, the coordinator mixes current_channel*w with previous_channel*(0x8000-w), using the held previous output during an interrupted transition, then normalizes by 0x8000 and clamps the result to 0..255. The weight 0x8000 is 1.0. Stock driving reachability of input modes 5 and 15 is unconfirmed on every image. The physical unit, engineering conversion and neutral value are unestablished; raw 128 is not qualified as neutral. No engine-bank identity is established. Editor values are stored counts; no engineering conversion is established.</description>
